<title>POLAND: ELEKTRIM REBOUNDS 4.6 PCT AFTER PLUNGE.</title>
<headline>ELEKTRIM REBOUNDS 4.6 PCT AFTER PLUNGE.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish industrial and trading conglomerate Elektrim SA, the main market's top gainer on Thursday, rebounded 4.6 percent to 25 zlotys after Wednesday's plunge on news the firm had revised down 1996 net profits.</p>
<p>The stock on Wednesday fell 9.8 percent after the firm revised down its 1996 net profit to 40.3 million from 49.8 million zlotys.</p>
<p>Traders said Elektrim, whose Thursday turnover was a session-high 19.3 million zlotys, should begin to stabilise along with the overall market.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
